---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="The Story — Punit Pal · IMPURE®" description="A developer, a student and the founder of Builder Base. Punit Pal’s journey through compiler experiments, AI systems and developer communities.">
  <div class="container editorial-page">
    <header class="story-intro">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Story / Punit Pal</p>
        <h1 class="editorial-title">Curiosity brought me<br />to the code.<br />People kept me here<span class="red-period">.</span></h1>
        <p class="editorial-intro">I’m a developer and the founder of Builder Base, studying Computer Science with a focus on AI and Data Science in Bhopal.</p>
      </div>
      <figure><img src="/images/punit-pal.webp" alt="Punit Pal in a city arcade" width="700" height="700" /><figcaption>India / Between code and community.</figcaption></figure>
    </header>
    <section class="story-chapter" aria-labelledby="building-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">01 / Building</p>
      <div><h2 id="building-title">Start with the friction.</h2>
        <p>I wanted to understand what happens between writing a program and running it. Smart contracts gave that curiosity a practical question: could a Python developer build on an EVM chain without starting over in another language?</p>
        <p>That became PyVax. Sol2Rust explores a different language boundary; FlowMon makes the connections between agents visible. Each project gives me another way to study the tools developers work with.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/build">Engineering notes ↗</a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="story-chapter" aria-labelledby="beyond-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">02 / Beyond code</p>
      <div><h2 id="beyond-title">Someone to build beside.</h2>
        <p>A useful tool still needs a way to reach people. I started Builder Base to bring developers closer to technical workshops, project opportunities and other builders.</p>
        <p>There’s a practical connection between the two: the questions people ask in a workshop help me see where a tool or its documentation needs work.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/grow">See the programs ↗</a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <figure class="story-community"><img src="/images/work/community-2.webp" width="1280" height="960" loading="lazy" alt="Claude Community participants gathered in an auditorium in Bhopal" /><figcaption>Claude Community, Bhopal. Photograph from <a href="https://www.builderbase.xyz/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Builder Base’s public photo archive ↗</a>.</figcaption></figure>
    <section class="story-chapter" aria-labelledby="milestones-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">03 / Milestones</p>
      <div><h2 id="milestones-title">A few points along the way.</h2>
        <ol class="story-timeline">
          <li><span>2024–2028</span><p>BTech in Computer Science Engineering, AI & Data Science at RGPV. Studies in progress.</p></li>
          <li><span>20 Dec 2025</span><p>Listed co-host of <a href="https://luma.com/pq4gfjtt" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">A Series All About Move ↗</a> at Galgotias University.</p></li>
          <li><span>28 Mar 2026</span><p>FlowMon at Monad Blitz V3. <a href="/build/flowmon">The project ↗</a> connects the engineering work with a Builder Base co-hosted event.</p></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="media-note">Education and project participation are owner-reported. Event dates and host credits are linked to public listings.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="https://impure.notion.site/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Full Proof of Work ↗</a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="story-chapter" aria-labelledby="now-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">04 / Now · October 2026</p>
      <div><h2 id="now-title">Still learning. Still building.</h2><p>Compiler tooling, agent workflows and developer programs through Builder Base. Alongside that, I’m continuing my 2024–2028 undergraduate degree.</p><a class="text-link" href="/contact">Get in touch ↗</a></div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .story-intro{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 260px;gap:70px;align-items:center}
  .story-intro img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;filter:grayscale(1)}
  .story-chapter{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;gap:70px;padding-top:32px;margin-top:72px;border-top:1px solid var(--editorial-rule)}
  .story-chapter h2{font:500 2.2rem/1.2 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.045em;margin-bottom:24px}
  .story-chapter p:not(.eyebrow){max-width:62ch;color:var(--text-muted);margin-bottom:20px}
  .story-community{margin:64px 0 0 25%;max-width:680px}.story-community img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}
  .story-community a,.story-timeline a{text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px}
  .story-timeline{list-style:none}.story-timeline li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:120px 1fr;gap:24px;border-top:1px solid var(--editorial-rule);padding-top:22px}.story-timeline span{font:500 .75rem/1.6 var(--font-mono);color:var(--text-muted)}
  @media(max-width:767px){.story-intro,.story-chapter{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:24px}.story-intro figure{width:180px;justify-self:end}.story-chapter{margin-top:48px}.story-community{margin:40px 0 0}.story-timeline li{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:10px}}
</style>
